Here is the code snippet of the `ebeMultiply` method in `OpenMapRealVector`:

```java
public OpenMapRealVector ebeMultiply(RealVector v) {
    checkVectorDimensions(v.getDimension());
    OpenMapRealVector res = new OpenMapRealVector(this);
    Iterator iter = res.entries.iterator();
    while (iter.hasNext()) {
        iter.advance();
        res.setEntry(iter.key(), iter.value() * v.getEntry(iter.key()));
    }
    return res;
}
```

The issue is likely happening in this line `res.setEntry(iter.key(), iter.value() * v.getEntry(iter.key()));` where `iter.key()` or `iter.value()` might be null causing a NullPointerException. 

